  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/... \nBy the end of the of the weekend and heading into the next work \nweek, global ensembles point towards H5 heights weakening slightly\nto between 594-597 dams, and the center of the anticyclone over \nAZ, stretching into the Four Corners region. Although these\nheights will still remain above the 90th percentile of \nclimatology for this time of year, resulting in temperatures \nremaining between 110F-114 in south central AZ, and the western \ndeserts between 113F-117F. Widespread Major to Extreme HeatRisk \nwill continue through Sunday, Major to localized Extreme Monday, \nand Moderate to localized Major by Tuesday. By Sunday moisture\nwill begin to increase once again, with easterly to northeasterly\nflow aloft which will have potential for increased chances of\nthunderstorm development in northeastern AZ, with current PoPs\nbetween 20-30% in eastern Gila County. Unfortunately, with this \noutlook being so far in advanced conditions may change, so further\nevaluation will be needed throughout the week.",
